{"seq":null,"source_sha256":"96a53dc84dd5f007cbaaa684980f0239e16cd02565651274c615f02204325e16","commit_to":{"owner":"pertson-labs","repo":"e2e-expert-repo","branch":"e2e-forget-1791717674597"},"doc_stem":"2026-10-11-2-forget-lifecycle-bystander","status":"completed","machine":{"spec_version":8,"spec_hash":"c492bc2a9086"},"checkpoint":"navigate","run_id":"mp-eng-030b375f","payload":{"expand_iris":[],"focus":"Onboarding process for new hires: Pallasine checklist, first-week accounts setup, pairing rotation, shadow shift, replacing the old wiki onboarding page; Wren Duskfield (Ops Lead)","rationale":"I called perspective once and checked every door it listed. The map and coverage hold only calibration material (the Kestrelwood spectrograph narrative, its one source document, and an unplaced calibration-settlement position), and the roster lists Quill Ashgrove, Xena ExpertGH, and an independent consultant, with no Wren Duskfield. The Documents and Unplaced doors show nothing on onboarding, checklists, accounts, pairing, or shadow shifts. The only focus-surfaced item, Decision_DiagnosticFirst, is about how engagements start with a diagnostic phase, which is a different subject, so I did not expand it as a reach. The Thematic and People doors returned NOT FOUND on the IRIs I tried, so I did not get a topic list from them. I expanded nothing, so the passes will see no graph content for this onboarding document.","n8n_execution_id":"159710","expansion_count":0,"context":"# Perspective — pertson-labs/e2e-expert-repo @ 6eed59893e0f45ca863f067ab8f4bf9b15458d2f\npin: 1684e6429ec354b5de5d4cd02defbb760091fc9c\n\nSections: (1) THE MAP — this graph's richest ground, full narration; (2) COVERAGE — what's active, contested, unplaced, and quiet across everything else, meaning inside whisper-brackets; (3) DOORS — complete axes (areas, people, dimensions, documents, unplaced), each one expand away; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map, coverage, and doors never vary with your focus.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nThis entry is BOUNDED — the whole graph is deliberately not inlined. Every node is reachable within a bounded number of expands: before concluding the perspective is silent on your subject, check the map and coverage, then expand the door whose axis would hold it (^Thematic for topics and areas, ^People for anyone, ^Documents for a call or memory, ^Unplaced for loose positions). Absence becomes signal only after the relevant door shows nothing.\n\n# The map — this graph's richest ground (top fidelity band)\n\n\n# Coverage — narrated, from four directions\n\nActive: [ Narrative_InstrumentCalibrationVerification · What reference evidence stands behind this instrument's calibrat… ^Narrative_InstrumentCalibrationVerification ] — the newest witnessed work, one document each.\nUnplaced (1): [ Position_CalibrationSettlementRecord · how does a verified calibration claim become a settled r… ^Position_CalibrationSettlementRecord ] — positions waiting for the narrative that makes them meaningful; ^Unplaced holds them all.\n\n# Doors — pick an axis\n\n[ ^Thematic — every area (0) by name ] [ ^People 3 ] [ ^Dimensions — 0 axes ] [ ^Documents 1 ] [ ^Unplaced 1 ]\nEach door expands to a complete axis: aswritten_expand(iris=[\"Thematic\"]) — same coords as this perspective. Nothing in the graph is outside every door.\n\n# Focus: Onboarding process for new hires: Pallasine checklist, first-week accounts setup, pairing rotation, shadow shift, replacing the old wiki onboarding page; Wren Duskfield (Ops Lead) (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n","positions":"Position_CalibrationSettlementRecord — how does a verified calibration claim become a settled record of decision in the memo?","pin":"1684e6429ec354b5de5d4cd02defbb760091fc9c","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[{\"name\":\"Position_CalibrationSettlementRecord\",\"frame\":\"how does a verified calibration claim become a settled record of decision in the memo?\",\"narratives\":[],\"unplaced\":true,\"challenges\":[],\"members\":[{\"iri\":\"Expr_20261011_1_ForgetLifecycleTarget_h3549e285340e_3\",\"excerpt\":\"Quill: \\\"The Kestrelwood spectrograph is now calibrated at 88.4 MHz.\\nWe verified the calibration against the June reference plates and it\\nholds across the full observing band.\\\"\"},{\"iri\":\"Expr_20261011_1_ForgetLifecycleTarget_h3549e285340e_5\",\"excerpt\":\"- **Instrument**: Kestrelwood spectrograph\\n- **Calibration**: 88.4 MHz, verified against June reference plates\"}],\"source\":null,\"role\":\"unplaced\"}]}","context_bytes":2759},"live_run_id":"a4f65402daed","at":"2026-10-11T11:22:37Z"}
